+# Paired local evaluation loop: brief
+
+Date: 2026-09-07. Task: v0a-evaluation-opening. Finalizer: Codex coordinator.
+Tier C: population identity, paired comparison, process ownership and evidence meaning.
+Base B: e043f81ecec3ac16128720b42c3312bb41a4ed67 in D:/Pontius.
+
+The controller said "Let's Begin" to preparing a bounded design and source-opening
+proposal for reproducible tables, matched baseline/blueprint comparisons and a clear
+report. This authorizes proposal work, not source implementation, evaluation cards,
+an evaluation run, source acceptance, a decision commit or remote publication.
+
+## Outcome and acceptance
+
+Deliver a CPU-only outer evaluation loop that compares baseline-rules-v1 against
+blueprint-v1 through the unchanged public session CLI. Each trial is one hand with
+fresh 200-chip stacks. The same full table bytes serve both strategies. Every planned
+deal/lineup covers all six controlled seats; starting button is configurable. This
+is a reusable correctness asset whose actual evaluation populations remain unadmitted.
+
+1. Strict canonical requests determine the complete ordered trial matrix before play.
+2. Existing seeded-deal recipe and four opponent scripts are reused unchanged.
+3. Every matched pair has identical cards, board, button, stacks and opponents; only
+   strategy/protocol/run identity differs. Six-seat rotation does not rotate away
+   relative position. Stack resets prevent policy-dependent dropout of later deals.
+4. Public session admission, legal engine, provider, fallback and action clock remain
+   authoritative. The parent never selects poker actions or delivers full deals to policy.
+5. A fresh create-only output root, per-trial intent and retained raw captures make
+   failures observable. No resume, retry, replacement arm, dropped row or silent success.
+6. Reports separate completed-pair chip deltas, applied action counts, provider fallback,
+   legacy blueprint choices, observed timing flags, action/hand/session failure scopes
+   and incomplete observations.
+7. Windows descendants are contained before executable work, captures have byte caps,
+   and one shared monotonic deadline governs trial admission and publication commit
+   verification. Postcommit guard release/visibility may occur later; no hard wall claim.
+8. Finite independent correctness controls and both supported interpreters establish
+   the machinery; no observed profitability is a source-acceptance gate.
+
+## Scope and ground truth
+
+Add two tools, three tests and one literal fixture, as named in source-contract.md.
+Only six existing registration files may change under exact prospective exceptions.
+No changes to src/pontius, host/session/generator, old tests other than the registration
+census, old fixtures, policies, transport or source-admission pins.
+The only permitted removal is the empty ephemeral publication guard after verified
+commit, as specified in the source contract; all retained files and roots remain.
+
+Ground truth: accepted B contracts and raw source for public CLI, dealing, reporting
+and native Job behavior; independently written literal matrices, counts and arithmetic
+for the new wrapper. Paired comparison is an experimental-design choice, not an
+optimal-poker oracle. Old displayed deals are not a development population.
+
+Seams: request/planner, fixed raw source loader, subprocess/native Job, session JSON
+and wire captures, raw retained artifacts, reducer, deadline and final publication.
+Only this evaluation increment depends on the proposal. Training, self-play, human
+play, GUI, new opponents, H32 and all previous consumed owners remain separate.
+
+## Budget and stop rule
+
+Production ceiling: 1,200 added lines across two new tools. Tests: 1,800 added lines;
+literal fixtures: 32 KiB. Manual registration: 160 added/removed lines, with generated
+inventory/profile bytes counted separately. Native process code is reused from the
+accepted host Job; no general scheduler, plugin system or new transport framework.
+The report reducer protects denominators and honest failure accounting, justifying
+its size within this cap. Split the design if these bounds cannot be met.
+
+One initial proposal/source candidate and up to three within-scope correction rounds
+at each stage. Preserve every round and review. A second residual on one contract
+requires the workflow root-cause/redesign treatment; source scope, population semantics,
+line budget or round-budget expansion returns to the controller. No source edits occur
+until the exact source-opening decision is adopted. Source acceptance/seal and actual
+evaluation launch each remain later separately authorized decisions.
+
+Proposal acceptance: freeze the six documentation paths, obtain two fresh independent
+Tier C reviews covering design and source contract, then status --check and all twelve
+status tests on actual 3.11.15 first and 3.14.6 second, each fresh D-local exact-candidate
+snapshot under the accepted scrubbed -B -P procedure. Verify base pins and no population
+creation. No poker/generator/inventory payload runs during this documentation task.
