+# ADR-0508: Open the paired local evaluation source round
+
+- Status: accepted source-opening decision upon its separately authorized commit
+- Date: 2026-09-07
+- Follows: ADR-0507
+- Base-Commit: e043f81ecec3ac16128720b42c3312bb41a4ed67
+- Invocation-Authority: finite named correctness controls after adoption; no evaluation run
+- Front-Door-Kind: controller-v1
+- Front-Door-Research: ADR-0280
+- Front-Door-Process: ADR-0508
+- Front-Door-Contract: ADR-0307
+- Front-Door-Revoked: ADR-0281, ADR-0468, ADR-0472, ADR-0475
+- Front-Door-Active-Next: Implement the bounded paired evaluation loop after exact adoption
+- Front-Door-Blockers: evaluation source acceptance pending; no evaluation population admitted
+
+## Decision
+
+Open the CPU-only paired local evaluation source increment under the brief, design
+and source-contract in docs/architecture/v0a-evaluation-r001/ and implementation plan
+docs/superpowers/plans/2026-09-07-paired-local-evaluation.md. The controller requested
+preparation of this bounded proposal; it has no effect until its exact decision
+commit is expressly authorized and made. No implementation occurs before adoption.
+
+The deliverable is a reproducible outer loop comparing baseline-rules-v1 and
+blueprint-v1 through the unchanged public session CLI. Each matched pair shares
+identical one-hand input, resets six 200-chip stacks, and uses the existing opponent
+scripts. Every deal/lineup covers all six seats. Alternating strategy order is fixed
+before outcomes. Source acceptance judges the comparison machinery, not profitability.
+
+Reports preserve applied actions, baseline fallback and legacy choice distinctions,
+timing observations, incomplete captures and separate action/hand/session failure
+observations. A complete aggregate requires
+the complete planned population; no survivor-only score or missing-as-zero result.
+Every partial attempt remains retained and cannot be resumed or rerolled. Whole-run
+deadline, native descendant containment and final publication have explicit contracts.
+The deadline covers verification of both closed/read-back final files and publication
+commit; subsequent visibility release and CLI return may be later. Consumers require
+the absent pending guard and fully validated bound files, not process exit alone.
+
+## Bounded source permissions
+
+Prospectively supersede CLAUDE rule 1 only for the six exact current registration
+blobs and limited changes in source-contract.md. Add exactly two stdlib tools,
+three finite correctness suites and one literal fixture named there. No src/pontius,
+existing host/session/generator, policy, old fixture, action clock, engine, transport
+or current source pin changes. The parent reuses accepted host.Job and the seeded
+recipe from exact verified raw buffers; child sessions retain their own source admission.
+Permit only the single postcommit removal of the empty .publication-pending resource
+specified in the contract. No retained file or consumed root may be deleted or recovered.
+
+Keep 1,200 new production lines, 1,800 new test lines, 160 manual registration
+added/removed lines and 32 KiB fixtures. Generated inventory/profile output and these
+documentation files are excluded from source line counts. One initial proposal and
+up to three within-scope corrections; one initial source candidate and up to three
+within-scope corrections. Preserve normal residual/root-cause rules and all rounds.
+Scope, budget or required source expansion needs a separate controller ruling.
+
+After adoption, permit only the finite named correctness controls and unchanged
+regressions in source-contract.md. They use at most two literal full deals, the one
+declared all-zero-seed correctness vector, and at most 24 actual session starts per
+execution of the new suite set. These tests may run only in fresh disposable D-local
+snapshots under the accepted scrubbed -B -P procedure, actual 3.11.15 first then3.14.6.
+No entropy, uncontrolled sampling, outcome-selected fixtures or evaluation follows.
+
+Two independent fresh Tier C CLEAN source reviews precede the sixteen listed
+acceptance commands on both actual interpreters. Preserve every old source byte
+outside the six exact exceptions, all old test IDs/assertions/order/grants and the
+full mechanically explained census. No analyzer repair, capability expansion or
+weakened gate is authorized. A separately reviewed source seal is a later decision.
+
+## Proposal acceptance and retained prior outcome
+
+This proposal changes exactly six paths: this ADR, brief.md, design.md,
+source-contract.md, the implementation plan and generated STATUS.md. Two fresh
+independent Tier C reviews cover the whole candidate's design and source-opening
+contract. Then run unchanged status --check and all twelve status tests on actual
+3.11.15 first then3.14.6, each fresh exact-candidate D-local snapshot. Verify raw base
+pins, exact scope and absence of new population/launch artifacts. No generator,
+poker, evaluation, inventory or source test runs during proposal preparation.
+
+ADR-0507's one generation and one baseline session are completed and consumed.
+All three hands completed with zero exit codes; the retained non-evidentiary
+disposition is D:/Pontius/tmp/v0a-baseline-watch-run-r001/final-disposition.json,
+SHA-256 2f9d99f1aaca32252680a80b80e9b7a0ef1ad6d51b9482af0b42d849b1382c5f.
+It establishes no playing-strength result and supplies no evaluation/tuning population.
+The source-opening task does not alter that owner or repeat its demonstration.
+
+Future population seed, lineups, size, resource budgets, metrics and interpretation
+must be fixed prospectively and separately authorized after source acceptance.
+Correctness-only namespaces and evidentiary=false remain unchanged in existing
+children. This opening grants no formal operation, actual comparative evaluation,
+calibration, demonstration, training, self-play, league, neural loading, new opponents,
+human play, GUI, H32, compiled work, analyzer repair, retained-artifact cleanup, export
+or ref retirement.
